WEBVTT

00:00:01.581 --> 00:00:13.401
PPRD East table-top exercise, with AI support. One phone plays every role: the Director, the Mayor, the Fire Commander and Regional Civil Protection.

00:00:13.453 --> 00:00:19.433
Each player picks a language. Regional Civil Protection will play in Armenian.

00:00:19.486 --> 00:00:27.746
The Director starts the exercise. Day 1, 13:00: a wildfire is burning on Pine Hill.

00:00:27.797 --> 00:00:35.417
The Director sends the first injects from the exercise script. The AI translates each one for its recipient.

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:45.530
The Mayor receives the injects in Italian: the fire, and 120 pupils at Pineta Primary School.

00:00:45.583 --> 00:00:49.763
The Mayor answers in Italian, in their own words.

00:00:52.713 --> 00:00:59.333
The Fire Commander orders fire lines using zone codes from the map grid, and an air-tanker drop.

00:01:02.312 --> 00:01:11.252
The AI turns each reply into commands, and the simulator checks every command against the role's authority and resources.

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:19.524
It flags a real constraint: evacuating 120 pupils needs 3 buses, but the Mayor has only 2.

00:01:19.576 --> 00:01:26.436
The Director writes an AI prompt: one extra bus for the Mayor, confirmed by an inject.

00:01:26.488 --> 00:01:33.988
The Director reviews the AI's proposal, a resource change plus an inject draft, and approves it.

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:38.700
The Fire Commander's orders are approved, with a note to the player.

00:01:38.752 --> 00:01:45.212
And the Mayor's orders now pass: 3 buses for 120 pupils.

00:01:45.262 --> 00:01:53.962
The Mayor gets exercise control's feedback in Italian.

00:01:54.013 --> 00:02:02.633
The Director resolves turn 1: thirty simulated minutes, played live on the big screen at 120 times speed.

00:02:02.685 --> 00:02:13.425
Flame length follows the fire's intensity and the share of Monte Carlo runs that burn each cell. The glow ahead is where only some runs reach.

00:02:13.477 --> 00:02:20.457
The fire lines are cut, the air tanker drops, and the school is evacuated to the sports centre.

00:02:20.509 --> 00:02:25.329
Every player gets an AI-written situation update for their role.

00:02:27.744 --> 00:02:40.724
Turn 2. The Director escalates: a wind warning, then commands by code, raising the wind to 55 km/h and starting a new fire in zone G5.

00:02:40.776 --> 00:02:50.836
Regional Civil Protection reads the wind warning in Armenian, and asks for international assistance through the EU Civil Protection Mechanism.

00:02:50.886 --> 00:02:54.266
A vague order from the Fire Commander…

00:02:55.103 --> 00:02:59.843
…gets a clarification question from the AI instead of a guess.

00:02:59.895 --> 00:03:03.435
The Fire Commander answers precisely.

00:03:04.838 --> 00:03:11.778
The Director rejects the vague order, and approves the assistance request and the precise fire lines.

00:03:20.210 --> 00:03:30.470
Turn 2 resolves live: sixty minutes. Reinforcements arrive, the lines protect Pineta, and the new fire spreads through the farmland.

00:03:53.185 --> 00:04:04.885
Every inject, reply, AI interpretation, decision and consequence is logged for the debrief. Humans decide; the AI mediates.

